ask(1862,'local-controller','Safe path following, supplied stopping-distance model','In a supplied one-dimensional model, a robot travels at 0.6 m/s, waits 0.2 s before braking, then decelerates at 0.9 m/s². A stationary obstacle is 0.40 m ahead of its leading boundary. What stopping distance and remaining clearance follow?', [('0.32 m stopping distance and 0.08 m clearance','Reaction travel is 0.12 m and braking travel 0.20 m; subtract their sum from 0.40 m.'),('0.20 m stopping distance and 0.20 m clearance','This ignores travel during the reaction delay.'),('0.52 m stopping distance and −0.12 m clearance','This omits the factor 2 in the braking-distance denominator.')],kind='numerical',difficulty='medium',ass=['All dynamics and distance supplied; constant-deceleration idealization only, not a measured controller safety guarantee.'],steps=['Reaction travel: 0.6×0.2=0.12 m.','Braking travel: 0.6²/(2×0.9)=0.20 m.','Total=0.32 m; remaining clearance=0.40−0.32=0.08 m.'],formulas=[STOP])
