ask(1863,'costmaps','Inflation-layer role, supplied footprint-margin exercise','A supplied planner requires 0.05 m clearance on each side of a circular robot of radius 0.20 m. A straight corridor is 0.45 m wide. Is the centered robot admissible under this rule?', [('No; the required width is 0.50 m, while the available side clearance is 0.025 m','The diameter is 0.40 m; the remaining 0.05 m is split between two sides.'),('Yes; 0.45 m exceeds the 0.40 m diameter, so the margin is automatically met','It fits geometrically but fails the additional 0.05 m-per-side requirement.'),('Yes; the full 0.05 m width difference is available on each side','The difference is total clearance, not the clearance on both sides independently.')],kind='numerical',difficulty='medium',ass=['All geometry and margin supplied; ideal centered circle; this is a clearance model, not the exact Nav2 inflation cost formula.'],steps=['Diameter=2×0.20=0.40 m.','Side clearance=(0.45−0.40)/2=0.025 m.','Required width=2×(0.20+0.05)=0.50 m, so reject.'],formulas=[CLEAR])
